# Vite loads this file automatically when running `vite` (dev) or `vite build
# --mode development`. It is the env baseline for `pnpm dev` and the playwright
# webServer used by `apps/e2e`. Production builds (`pnpm build` from `apps/web`)
# do NOT load this file.
#
# Feature flags here are intentionally permissive so developers see in-flight
# surfaces without manual setup. Use `.env.development.local` (gitignored) to
# override for your machine. Production gating lives in deploy-time env.

# For You sparse-state composer (bet `foryou-sparse-composer`).
# `*` enables every workspace in dev / e2e so AC-U1/U2/U4 specs render the
# composer against a fresh test workspace whose UUID isn't known up front.
# Production overrides this with the explicit founders allowlist.
VITE_FORYOU_COMPOSER_WORKSPACES=*
